1
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:04,360
<i>Do you remember the legend of the tree</i>
<i>that proves true love?</i>

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:06,560
<i>If a couple kisses under this tree</i>
<i>and they're meant for each other,</i>

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,600
<i>they will stay together.</i>

4
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:11,240
<i>After the kiss,</i>
<i>whether we feel something or nothing,</i>

5
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,120
<i>we both have to say it honestly.</i>

6
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,680
One. Two. Three.

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,080
- - I felt something.
- I felt something.

8
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:00,240
Are you awake?

9
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,520
How are you feeling? Tired?

10
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,720
I'm still a little wiped out.

11
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,880
My legs ache too.

12
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,640
Of course you're exhausted.

13
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:21,160
You got lost in the woods last night.

14
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:26,520
Go take a shower.
They'll probably gather everyone soon.

15
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:28,080
I'll pack your things for you.

16
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,880
Do you really have to do all this?

17
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,800
Do what?

18
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:47,800
I'm just acting like someone
you've allowed to win you over.

19
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:55,000
Last night, I made you
lose your way in the woods.

20
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:00,880
This time…

21
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:05,440
I'll make you fall for me.

22
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,000
Fall for you, my ass!

23
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,000
I'm going to take a shower.

24
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,080
How are you feeling?

25
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:05,080
Did you and I…

26
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,320
I thought I was dreaming.

27
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:13,640
I thought it was a dream.

28
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:15,320
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to do it.

29
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:19,240
I shouldn't have done that to you
while I was drunk.

30
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:23,640
Fine. Just forget it.

31
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,000
Don't overthink it.

32
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:27,720
Consider it…

33
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,440
a one-night stand.

34
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:35,160
I won't say anything,
and you won't either.

35
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,200
That's all.

36
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,880
- Well…
- Don't overthink it.

37
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:45,080
What we have is just a situationship.

38
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:17,200
<i>Will you be my boyfriend?</i>

39
00:04:17,279 --> 00:04:19,880
- Yeah.
- Really?

40
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:35,600
I will never be like you, Rin.

41
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:51,040
Hey!

42
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:02,720
About everyone
searching for you last night…

43
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:05,320
You weren't acting, were you?

44
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:10,040
Not everyone sees everything
as content as you do.

45
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:13,600
What's really going on between
you and Khobfa? What about Krit?

46
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:16,280
- You flirted with Krit to get his help.
- I didn't.

47
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,920
If you're sure you don't like him,
then end things cleanly.

48
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:22,560
I've already cut him off.

49
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:27,560
But can your guy do the same?

50
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:31,720
I know you can cut people off.
You're good at it.

51
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:35,720
You cut off your entire group
of close friends before.

52
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:41,120
I'm ready. Are you?

53
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,440
Rin.

54
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,960
Are you done? Shall we go now?

55
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:50,480
- Hold on!
- Hold on!

56
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:56,800
Here we go.
We even got the sea in the shot.

57
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:59,080
Smile.

58
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:18,080
Should I carry that for you?

59
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:42,680
So Rin, what's the deal with you two?

60
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:46,000
You two are acting weird.

61
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:48,400
You've defined your relationship,
haven't you?

62
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:50,240
No.

63
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:53,240
Khobfa just asked if he could win me over.

64
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,920
Seriously?

65
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,720
Are you pulling tricks on him again?

66
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:58,840
Exactly.

67
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:01,640
Jeez. Why would I?

68
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,960
- We already kissed.
- What?

69
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,160
Well…

70
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:13,600
I guess the True Love Tree
really does work.

71
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:14,920
- Yeah.
- It's holy, right?

72
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,960
- It really is. Awesome.
- Yeah.

73
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:19,040
- Come on, let's go!
- That was hard.

74
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,720
- He's shy.
- Shy, huh? Come on.

75
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:24,320
- Hey, can I hold it too?
- Let me hold your hand too!

76
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Is the AC blowing on you?

77
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,600
Hey.

78
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,240
About last night…

79
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:01,600
- I…
- What song did you send me?

80
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:09,880
I listened to it and thought of you,

81
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:11,240
so I shared it with you.

82
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,240
Here, give it a listen.

83
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:26,360
I'm going to rest my eyes.

84
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,600
I barely slept last night.

85
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:32,200
I'll listen to it when I wake up.

86
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:35,720
Okay.

87
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:09,480
Wow!

88
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:15,720
Khobfa, order whatever you want.

89
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,040
This meal is on us.

90
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:20,360
Yeah. Consider it our way of thanking you

91
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:23,880
for keeping our beloved friend safe.

92
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:28,720
Come to think of it,

93
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:32,120
this is the first time
we've really gotten to talk to you.

94
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:35,040
We'd like to get to know you better.

95
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:38,640
So, can we interview you?

96
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:41,680
- I'll ask the first question.
- Go ahead.

97
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:45,920
Why did you choose
to study business administration?

98
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,400
Jeez!

99
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,320
That's such a formal question.

100
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:51,520
Can you ask something more creative?

101
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,080
I like this field,

102
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,960
and I want to have
my own business someday.

103
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:59,440
Jeez.

104
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:02,480
Next question.

105
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:05,040
How many people have you dated?

106
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:07,360
That's a bold question, dude.

107
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:19,680
What is that?

108
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,720
Zero. I've never been in a relationship.

109
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:24,000
- What?
- Huh?

110
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:27,280
Someone like you has never dated anyone?
That's hard to believe.

111
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:32,800
Dig in.

112
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:47,520
Well, I'm going to use the restroom.

113
00:11:57,040 --> 00:12:00,440
You and Rin are roommates.
Do you two ever fight?

114
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:03,040
Do you take good care of Rin
when you're together?

115
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:05,560
Has he ever been unreasonable with you?

116
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:18,440
I have something to confess.

117
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:20,520
I asked Rin if I could win him over.

118
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,920
- What a surprise!
- Such a surprise!

119
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,400
- Yeah.
- Actually…

120
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,240
We already knew.

121
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:31,600
- How did you know?
- How could we not?

122
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,960
We've known from the start, dude.

123
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:41,960
I’ll do everything I can for him.

124
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:45,160
But if I ever make him uncomfortable,
I'll back off.

125
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,680
- No way!
- No way!

126
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:49,520
Don't you dare back off, Khobfa.

127
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:52,040
Now that you've made your move,
there's no turning back.

128
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,640
Exactly.

129
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:56,920
If you have a problem with our friend
or don't understand him,

130
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,440
just tell us and we'll coach you.

131
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:01,520
Rin isn't that complicated.

132
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:03,440
Just don't spoil him too much.

133
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:04,600
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

134
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:08,800
Since we're at it,
let's make a toast to Khobfa.

135
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:11,160
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

136
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:14,480
Hey. What are you toasting to?
Why didn't you wait for me?

137
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,680
You're back! Come join the toast.

138
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:18,040
- Come on. Cheers!
- Come on.

139
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:21,040
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

140
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:33,480
<i>Do you want to talk?</i>
<i>It can be about anything.</i>

141
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:37,200
But it's okay if you don't want to.
I know that's just how you are.

142
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:39,160
Do whatever you're comfortable with.

143
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:43,480
So why do you like drawing?

144
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:46,440
Wow. You're really asking me that?

145
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:49,040
When I was little, I only drew for fun.

146
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,840
Then someone saw my drawings
and said they were good.

147
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:56,840
That made me think I was good at it,
so I kept drawing.

148
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:58,560
And I grew to love it.

149
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:00,920
It's really nice, though.

150
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:05,880
Whenever I feel something so strongly
that I can't put into words,

151
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:07,960
I just draw it.

152
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:12,280
It's like capturing that feeling
in a picture and preserving it.

153
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:27,160
Hey. Sneaking a photo of me, huh?

154
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:29,400
Let me see.

155
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:31,320
Do I look good?

156
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:32,840
Okay.

157
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:36,000
Let's take a selfie
so we'll have a photo together.

158
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:45,200
But it's okay if you're uncomfortable.

159
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:47,880
No, I'm not uncomfortable.

160
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:52,800
I've just never taken a selfie
with someone I'm hitting on before.

161
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:57,600
Then I'm your first.

162
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:03,400
Come on. You should practice
so you'll get used to it.

163
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:20,040
Is something wrong?

164
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:21,920
You're the one acting strange.

165
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,280
You've been avoiding me
since we got back from Rayong

166
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,720
and ignoring my messages.

167
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:28,920
I've been busy with work lately.

168
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,160
It's about that night, isn't it?

169
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:40,760
You're avoiding me because of that night.

170
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:43,320
What do you want me to do? Just tell me.

171
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:45,000
Don't overthink it.

172
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:46,840
We both had fun that night.

173
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:50,560
That makes us even.
We don't owe each other anything.

174
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:53,480
I have more work to do. I should go.

175
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:01,000
Can I sleep in your room tonight?

176
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:09,400
I think you should sleep
in your own room tonight.

177
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:22,680
Hey, give me your phone.
I'll send it to myself.

178
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:26,440
There, done.

179
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:32,560
Aren't you embarrassed

180
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:35,480
to post me on your story?

181
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:39,000
No. I set it to "close friends" only.

182
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:43,520
There, it's posted.

183
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:47,440
You added me to your "close friends"?

184
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:02,080
Sneaky. You're being sneaky.

185
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:03,880
Come on.

186
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:22,760
Hey, what are you doing?

187
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:28,720
From now on, you can sleep in my bed
whenever you want.

188
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,160
What?

189
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:44,360
Are you uncomfortable?

190
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,000
No.

191
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:51,760
I just realized a king-sized bed
is perfect for two people.

192
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:07,800
Ouch!

193
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:14,280
Good night.

194
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:21,680
I know you're secretly smiling.

195
00:18:23,120 --> 00:18:24,320
No, I'm not!

196
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:51,960
From now on,
it's going to be just the two of us.

197
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:54,440
Your dad has passed away.

198
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:00,480
<i>Don't accept it, Mom.</i>

199
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:01,800
<i>Don't accept it, Mom.</i>

200
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:05,000
<i>Our family has a mystical lineage.</i>

201
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,200
<i>If you choose to inherit it,</i>

202
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:08,680
<i>- you must prepare to be unlucky in love.</i>
- Don't accept it, Mom.

203
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:10,080
<i>Don't accept it, Mom.</i>

204
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:13,800
<i>- Once you inherit it, if you fall in love,</i>
<i>- Please don't accept it.</i>

205
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:18,320
<i>fate will take that person away from you.</i>

206
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,480
I'm not going to lose you too, am I?

207
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:36,680
Is something wrong?

208
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:39,720
I just had a little nightmare.

209
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:45,320
I don't think these pillows

210
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:47,680
are doing a very good job.

211
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:55,320
So tonight, I'll be your pillow.

212
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:58,360
Hug me instead.

213
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:02,360
I'll hold you so tightly…

214
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:07,840
that you can't go anywhere.

215
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:22,920
<i>All right, everyone.</i>

216
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:25,800
For your midterm assignment,

217
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:31,240
I'd like you to create a drawing
based on the theme "A Painful Memory."

218
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:34,440
Draw it however you like.

219
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:38,600
Any style is fine,
as long as it fits the theme.

220
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:44,480
<i>If you fall in love,</i>
<i>fate will take that person away from you.</i>

221
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:45,600
<i>Let's part ways.</i>

222
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:47,440
I don't think I can do this anymore.

223
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:56,800
Look over there.

224
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:58,760
Prof. James's star pupil.

225
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:01,720
He looks ready to submit his work already.
Look at his face.

226
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:04,720
Come on, Rin.
You came emotionally prepared, huh?

227
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:06,800
Your head must be full of ideas.

228
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:11,280
You're not the only one aiming for an A.
Share your ideas with us.

229
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:13,080
Right. I can't think of anything.

230
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:32,160
<i>How is it going?</i>

231
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:33,920
<i>Have you come up with anything?</i>

232
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:38,880
I've thought of a way to help you.

233
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:43,320
First, slowly close your eyes

234
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:45,880
and think of the saddest moment
in your life.

235
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:49,240
<i>Let your mind go wherever it takes you.</i>

236
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:53,640
<i>Whatever you see first</i>
<i>is probably the one.</i>

237
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:57,560
<i>- Don't accept it, Mom.</i>
<i>- Our family has a mystical lineage.</i>

238
00:21:57,640 --> 00:22:01,080
<i>If you choose to inherit it,</i>
<i>you must prepare to be unlucky in love.</i>

239
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:04,560
<i>So you've been hiding</i>
<i>this whole mystical family thing from me?</i>

240
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:08,560
No, Khobfa.

241
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:09,560
No!

242
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:13,000
Why did you hide it from me?

243
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:18,560
You were afraid I wouldn't date you,
right?

244
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:21,320
You were right.

245
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:24,000
I'm already forcing myself
to stay with you.

246
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:28,800
I regret ever trusting you.

247
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:33,520
Get out!

248
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:36,040
Khobfa!

249
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:37,760
Please listen to me, Khobfa!

250
00:22:37,840 --> 00:22:40,240
Khobfa! Listen to me!

251
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:42,680
Khobfa!

252
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:43,720
Rin!
Rin!

253
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:48,000
Rin!
Rin!

254
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:53,240
It's ready. Let's eat.
It's ready. Let's eat.

255
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:01,800
How are the noodles?
How are the noodles?

256
